.\"t
.\" Automatically generated by Pandoc 1.18
.\"
.TH "alter" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
alter \- modify the properties of the collection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]db.collectionspace.collection.alter(<options>)\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
SdbCollection
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to modify the properties of the collection.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
options ( \f[I]object, required\f[] )
.PP
Modify the collection properties through the parameter "options":
.IP \[bu] 2
ReplSize ( \f[I]number\f[] ): The number of replicas that need to be
synchronized for write operations, and the default value is 1, which means that
write operations only need to be written to the master node.
.RS 2
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
\-1: The write request needs to be synchronized to a number of active nodes in
the replication group before the database write operation returns a response to
the client.
.IP \[bu] 2
0: The write request needs to be synchronized to all nodes in the replication
group before the database write operation returns a response to the client.
.IP \[bu] 2
1~7: The write request needs to be synchronized to the specified number of nodes
in the replication group before the database write operation returns a response
to the client.
.PP
Format: \f[C]ReplSize: 0\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
ShardingKey ( \f[I]object\f[] ): Sharding key, and the value is 1 or \-1,
indicating f orward or reverse sorting.
.RS 2
.PP
"ShardingKey" can be modified when the collection only exists in one data group,
or the collection does not have subcollections mounted.
.PP
Format: \f[C]ShardingKey: {<field1>: <1|\-1>, [<field2>: <1|\-1>, ...]}\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
ShardingType ( \f[I]string\f[] ): Sharding type, and the default value is
"hash".
.RS 2
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
"hash": Hash sharding.
.IP \[bu] 2
"range": Range sharding.
.PP
"ShardingType" can be modified when the collection only exists in one data
group.
.PP
Format: \f[C]ShardingType: "range"\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Partition ( \f[I]number\f[] ): The number of sharding, and the default value is
4096.
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
The value of this parameter must be a power of 2, and the range is [2^3, 2^20].
.IP \[bu] 2
This parameter can only take effect when the value of the parameter
"ShardingType" is "hash".
.IP \[bu] 2
"Partition" can be modified when the collection only exists in one data group.
.PP
Format: \f[C]Partition: 512\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
AutoSplit ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to enable the automatic segmentation
function, and the default value is "false", which means that automatic
segmentation is not enabled.
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
This parameter can only take effect when the value of the parameter
"ShardingType" is "hash".
.IP \[bu] 2
"AutoSplit" can be modified when the collection only exists in one data group.
.PP
Format: \f[C]AutoSplit: true\f[]
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[]
.PP
User can specify the parameter "AutoSplit" when creating domains and
collections.
If user explicitly specify "AutoSplit" for a collection, the system will give
priority to determining whether to enable automatic splitting according to the
value specified by the collection.
.RE
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
EnsureShardingIndex ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to automatically create an
index named "$shard" according to the field specified by the parameter
"ShardingKey", and the default value is "true", which means automatically
created.
.RS 2
.PP
"EnsureShardingIndex" can be modified when the collection only exists in one
data group.
.PP
Format: \f[C]EnsureShardingIndex: false\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Compressed ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to enable the data compression
function, and the default value is "true", which means that the data compression
function is enable.
.RS 2
.PP
Format: \f[C]Compressed: false\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
CompressionType ( \f[I]string\f[] ): Compression algorithm type, and the default
value is "lzw".
.RS 2
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
"snappy": Snappy algorithm compression.
.IP \[bu] 2
"lzw": Lzw algorithm compression.
.PP
Format: \f[C]CompressionType: "snappy"\f[]
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[]
.PP
For the usage scenarios of "snappy" compression and "lzw" compression, please
refer to data compression.
.RE
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
StrictDataMode ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to enable strict data type mode,
and the default value is "false", which means it is not enable.
.RS 2
.PP
After enabling strict mode, if the data type is numeric, an error will be
reported if an overflow occurs during the operation.
If the data type is not numeric, no operation will be performed.
.PP
Format: \f[C]StrictDataMode: true\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
AutoIncrement ( \f[I]object\f[] ): Properties of auto\-incrementing field.
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
The properties that are allowed to be modified can refer to the auto\-increment
field.
.IP \[bu] 2
After modifying the attribute, the field value may not be unique.
If users need to ensure that the modified value is unique, it is recommended to
use a unique index.
.PP
Format: \f[C]AutoIncrement: {Field: <Field name>, ...}\f[] or
\f[C]AutoIncrement: [{Field: <Field name1>, ...}, {Field: <Field name2>, ...}, ...]\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
AutoIndexId ( \f[I]boolean\f[] )：Identifies whether to create $id index.
.RS 2
.PP
格式：\f[C]AutoIndexId: true | false\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
DSMainCLName ( \f[I]string\f[] )：The related main collection name of collection
at data source.
.RS 2
.PP
Only valid when a data source collection is attached as a sub\-collection.
If the main\-collection name related with collection at data source end does not
match the actual name, this option can be used to correct it.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[]
.IP \[bu] 2
The specific way of using each option can refers to createCL().
.IP \[bu] 2
The partition collection cannot modify the attributes related to the partition,
such as "ShardingKey", "Partition".
.IP \[bu] 2
"EnsureShardingIndex" and "AutoSplit" are only effective for the current
operation, and only effective when modifying partition properties, such as
"ShardingKey".
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
AutoIndexId ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to automatically create a unique index
named "$id" based on the field "_id", and the default value is "true", which me
ans automatically created.
.RS 2
.PP
Format: \f[C]AutoIndexId: false\f[]
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, there is no return value.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
